{"_id":{"$oid":"5c4670cd08d98a02694c5455"},"headword":"אָבַד","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"A00030","language_code":"(b. h.;","refs":["Sifrei Devarim 301","Bereishit Rabbah 91:9","Ketubot 108a:2","Ketubot 104a","Sifrei Devarim 301","Nedarim 33b:3","Avodah Zarah 55a:5","Avodah Zarah 55a:6","Mishnah Avodah Zarah 4:7","Chagigah 3a:17","Chagigah 4a:1","Bereishit Rabbah 82","Jerusalem Talmud Sheviit 9:1:11"],"language_reference":" √<a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_אָב I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, אָב I 1\">אב</a>","content":{"senses":[{"definition":" , v. <span dir=\"rtl\">אבב</span>) <i>to be pressed, go around in despair</i> (v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Proverbs.31.6\" data-ref=\"Proverbs 31:6\">Prov. XXXI, 6</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.26.6\" data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 26:6\">Deut. XXVI, 6</a>) <i>to be given up</i>, whence "},{"definition":"<i>to be lost, perish; to be beyond recognition</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sifrei_Devarim.301\" data-ref=\"Sifrei Devarim 301\">Sifré Deut. 301</a> (ref. to <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.26.5\" data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 26:5\">Deut. XXVI, 5</a>) <span dir=\"rtl\">לא ירד … אלא לאובד</span> (read <span dir=\"rtl\">לוֹבֵד</span> or <span dir=\"rtl\">לֶאֱבוֹד</span>; Yalk. Deut. a. l. <span dir=\"rtl\">לאבדם</span> prob. <span dir=\"rtl\">לאַבְרָּן</span>; Ms. Zer. Abr. 3 <span dir=\"rtl\">לֵיאָבֵר</span>) Jacob went to Aram with no hope but to perish (be a slave &c.). Ohol. XVII, 3 a field <span dir=\"rtl\">שא׳ בו קבר</span> in which there is a grave that cannot be located. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Ketubot.13.7\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Ketubot 13:7\">Keth. XIII, 7</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אָבְדָה דרך וכ׳</span> the path to his field cannot be traced. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bereishit_Rabbah.91.9\" data-ref=\"Bereishit Rabbah 91:9\">Gen. R. s. 91</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אבידה א׳ לנו</span> we have lost something; a. fr.","number":"1)"},{"definition":"<i>to lose</i>. Ib. <span dir=\"rtl\">ואנו שאָבַדְנוּ ר׳ ס׳</span> and we who have lost (mourn for) R. S.; a. fr.—Part. pass. <span dir=\"rtl\">אָבוּד</span> <i>lost, irretrievable, perishing, decayed</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Ketubot.108a.2\" data-ref=\"Ketubot 108a:2\">Keth. 108ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">על הא׳</span> on a contribution to the Temple which has been lost on the road. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Sheviit.9.1.11\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Sheviit 9:1:11\">Y. Shebi. IX, 38ᵈ</a> top <span dir=\"rtl\">מאיליהן הן אֲבוּדִין</span> they perish of themselves (they decay naturally); a. fr.","number":"—2)"},{"grammar":{"binyan_form":["נֶאֱבַד"],"verbal_stem":"Nif."},"senses":[{"definition":"<i>to be lost, perish</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Ketubot.104a\" data-ref=\"Ketubot 104a\">Keth. 104ᵃ</a>; a. fr. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sifrei_Devarim.301\" data-ref=\"Sifrei Devarim 301\">Sifré Deut. 301</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">לֵיאָבֵד</span>, v. supra."}]},{"grammar":{"binyan_form":["אִיבֵּד"],"verbal_stem":"Pi."},"senses":[{"definition":"<i>to waste, lose, forfeit, destroy</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Nedarim.33b.3\" data-ref=\"Nedarim 33b:3\">Ned. 33ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אי׳ את מעותיו</span> he wasted his money, (cannot reclaim it). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Ketubot.13.6\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Ketubot 13:6\">Keth. XIII, 6</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אי׳ את זכותו</span> he forfeited his claim. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Avodah_Zarah.55a.6\" data-ref=\"Avodah Zarah 55a:6\">Ab. Zar. 55ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אנו נְאַבֵּד וכ׳</span> shall we give up our honest dealing? <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Avodah_Zarah.4.7\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Avodah Zarah 4:7\">Ib. IV, 7</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">יְאַבֵּד עולמו</span> shall He destroy His world? <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Chagigah.3a.17\" data-ref=\"Chagigah 3a:17\">Ḥag. 3ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ובקשתם לאַבְּדָהּ ממני</span> and you wanted to deprive me of it? <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Chagigah.4a.1\" data-ref=\"Chagigah 4a:1\">Ib. 4ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">זה המְאַבֵּד וכ׳</span> one who destroys what is given to him.—א׳ עצמו לדעת <i>to commit suicide wilfully</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bereishit_Rabbah.82\" data-ref=\"Bereishit Rabbah 82\">Gen. R. s. 82</a>; a. fr.","number":"1)"},{"definition":"<i>to drop from memory, to forget.</i> <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Pirkei_Avot.5.12\" data-ref=\"Pirkei Avot 5:12\">Aboth V, 12</a>; a. e.","number":"—2)"}]}]},"plural_form":[],"alt_headwords":[],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"אבגרוטינה","next_hw":"אֲבַּד"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c4670cd08d98a02694c5468"},"headword":"אֲבַּד","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"A00031","language_code":" ch. ","refs":["Sanhedrin 111a","Bereishit Rabbah 56:11","Vayikra Rabbah 34:12","Pesachim 5b","Eichah Rabbah 4","Jerusalem Talmud Pesachim 9:6:11"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<i>to be lost</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_I_Samuel.9.3\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on I Samuel 9:3\">Targ. I Sam. IX, 3</a>; a. fr.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sanhedrin.111a\" data-ref=\"Sanhedrin 111a\">Snh. 111ᵃ</a>; a. fr.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Pesachim.9.6.11\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Pesachim 9:6:11\">Y. Pes. IX, 37ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">כאָבִיד הוא</span> it is to be looked upon as lost."},{"grammar":{"binyan_form":["אַבַּד"],"verbal_stem":"Pa."},"senses":[{"definition":"<i>to destroy</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_II_Kings.19.18\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on II Kings 19:18\">Targ. II Kings, XIX, 18</a>; a. fr."}]},{"grammar":{"binyan_form":["אוֹבֵד"," אוֹבֵיד"],"verbal_stem":"Af."},"senses":[{"definition":" = <i>Pa.</i> <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Onkelos_Deuteronomy.26.5\" data-ref=\"Onkelos Deuteronomy 26:5\">Targ. Deut. XXVI, 5</a>; a. fr.—Y. Kidd. III, 64ᶜ bot. <span dir=\"rtl\">אובדתא חיין וכ׳</span> thou hast ruined this man’s (my) life. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bereishit_Rabbah.56.11\" data-ref=\"Bereishit Rabbah 56:11\">Gen. R. s. 56</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אובדת ליבך</span> thou hast lost thy wits; a. fr.","number":"1)"},{"definition":"<i>to be lost, to go to ruin</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Psalms.41.6\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Psalms 41:6\">Targ. Ps. XLI, 6</a>; a. e.—Y. Ḥag. II, 77ᵇ <span dir=\"rtl\">ווי דמובדין</span> alas for the lost (deceased)! Y. M. Kat. I, beg. 80ᵃ <span dir=\"rtl\">ויובדן</span> and decay.","number":"—2)"}]},{"grammar":{"binyan_form":["אִתְאַבַּד"],"verbal_stem":"Ithpa."},"senses":[{"definition":"<i>to be lost</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Vayikra_Rabbah.34.12\" data-ref=\"Vayikra Rabbah 34:12\">Lev. R. s. 34</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מִתְאַבְּדִין</span> if they should be lost.—<span dir=\"rtl\">מִתְּבִיד</span> = <span dir=\"rtl\">מִתְאֲבִיד</span> <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Pesachim.5b\" data-ref=\"Pesachim 5b\">Pes. 5ᵇ</a>; a. e. [<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Eichah_Rabbah.4\" data-ref=\"Eichah Rabbah 4\">Lam. R., to IV, 21</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">לאיבדא</span>, read <span dir=\"rtl\">לאיעבדא</span>, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עֲבַד.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עֲבַד 1\">עֲבַד</a>.]"}]}]},"plural_form":[],"alt_headwords":["אָבַד"],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"אָבַד","next_hw":"אָבֵד"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c4671f608d98a02694c5b59"},"headword":"אָדַם","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"A00417","language_code":"(b. h.;","refs":["Jastrow, דָּמַם 1","Bamidbar Rabbah 9:21","Chullin 53b","Bamidbar Rabbah 4:8","Bamidbar Rabbah 4:20","Shabbat 156a"],"language_reference":" √<a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_דָּם.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, דָּם 1\">דם</a>","content":{"senses":[{"definition":" , v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_דָּמַם.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, דָּמַם 1\">דמם</a>) [<i>to be viscous, thick, dark</i>] <i>to be red, grow red</i>."},{"grammar":{"binyan_form":["אִדֵּם"],"verbal_stem":"Pi."},"senses":[{"definition":"<i>to redden, make red</i>. Y. Sabb. VII, 10ᶜ top <span dir=\"rtl\">המְאַדֵּם אודם</span> he who produces a red spot (congestion of blood, on a Sabbath)."}]},{"grammar":{"binyan_form":["הֶאֱדִים"],"verbal_stem":"Hif."},"senses":[{"definition":" (b. h.) (b. h.) <i>to be, grow red</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bamidbar_Rabbah.9.21\" data-ref=\"Bamidbar Rabbah 9:21\">Num. R. s. 9</a> (p. 231ᵇ ed. Amst.) <span dir=\"rtl\">מַאֲדֶמֶת</span> (<span dir=\"rtl\">היתה</span>) if she was red-faced. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Chullin.53b\" data-ref=\"Chullin 53b\">Ḥull. 53ᵇ</a>; a. fr.","number":"1)"},{"definition":"<i>to cause to blush, put to shame</i> (usu. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_לָבַן II.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, לָבַן II 1\">הלבין</a>). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bamidbar_Rabbah.4.20\" data-ref=\"Bamidbar Rabbah 4:20\">Num. R. s. 4</a> (p. 218ᵈ ed. Amst.) (play on <span dir=\"rtl\">עובד אדום</span>).—<i>Part.</i> מַאֲדִים <i>the planet Mars</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Shabbat.156a\" data-ref=\"Shabbat 156a\">Sabb. 156ᵃ</a>.—<i>Part. Hof</i>. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְאָדָּם</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מְאוּדָּם</span>. Y. Sabb. VII, 10ᶜ top <span dir=\"rtl\">מְאָדָּמִים</span> dyed red.","number":"—2)"}]}]},"plural_form":[],"alt_headwords":[],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"אֲדַם","next_hw":"אָדָם"}
